// RESOLVED (Eric's ruling 2026-08-13, option A): the fold is a
// function of (source, init, callback) — bottom in, bottom out. A
// consuming callback's bottom taints its slot and travels the acc
// chain (FreshBottom on the triggering delivery, quiet ride on the
// standing one); an acc-ignoring callback recovers organically.
// `held` survives as sleep/frame memory but never substitutes for a
// poisoned production. The interp's ride-Stale behavior was the
// FoldQ slot walk's held-history ride branch — a pre-dense fork-7
// residual contradicting the intent comment beside it; the kernel
// was right all along. The accumulator now advances only on good
// cycles in BOTH engines (0,100,200 at alternate epochs). MapQ's
// twin branch STAYS: map slots are op-sites where the kernel's
// in-loop taint-cache words genuinely ride — probed AGREE.
//
// aug13b reactive class (hz0-re 000005/000013/000014 + shape-family
// 000002/000003/000006, hz1-re 000001): a fold whose INIT arg bottoms
// on alternate cycles (100 / (x % 3) at x=0).
//
// INTERP (canonical): the tainted init's FRESH_BOTTOM acc delivery
// (collection.rs ~1190) is GATED TO SILENCE at the callback CallSite
// (the taint-gate: poison never dispatches a callee), so the slot
// stays quiet and the fold delivers Stale(resident) — the value
// channel advances, and a `~`-sampled connect accumulator grows EVERY
// cycle: v1 = 0,100,200,300,400.
// NOTE: this CONTRADICTS the intent comment at the FRESH_BOTTOM
// insert ("a consuming callback taints its slot and the
// any-slot-tainted check bottoms the fold") — the gate silences the
// delivery before any slot can consume it. Comment or behavior is
// wrong; adjudicate which.
//
// KERNEL: the fold's acc chain taints (FoldAcc carries the init
// taint), the region result taints, the boundary forces absence, the
// sample's held arg rides its LAST GOOD sum — the bottom cycle's
// accumulation is LOST: v1 = 0,100,200 (every other cycle).
//
// If the interp is ruled right, the kernel needs a RIDE at the fold
// result seam (tainted-with-history result delivers the ridden value
// STALE — the scrut/guard-ride pattern at the loop's result disc).
// If the comment is ruled right, the interp's gate must except
// FoldQ's own acc chain. Either way one engine changes; parked for
// the ruling.
{
    let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:0, i64:1, i64:0]);
    let v1 = i64:0;
    let v3: i64 = array::fold([false], i64:100 / (x % i64:3), |v4, v5| v4);
    v1 <- x ~ v1 + v3;
    v1
}
